<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    looptest, the zero-trip guard drop: a guard in front of a rotated loop is
    dropped when the program without it is the same on the skip path.

    Issue: kuna-looptest3 (decbench O2: gcc copies the loop test into a guard
    and gives the skip path its own copy of the code after the loop, so kuna
    printed `if (c) { do ... while (c); return x; } return 0;` where the source
    has one top-tested loop).  Stage P8 (goto-quality), P0 assertion
    `option looptest binary|proven|assume` (default `proven`).

    The bytes are .text of authored C built by gcc 11.4 -O2 -fno-inline
    -fcf-protection=none, linked at 0x100000 with the helpers report, keep and
    release:
      dsum          s = 0; for (i = 0; i < n; i++) s += a[i]; return s;
                    (skip path `return 0.0`, the exit `return s`)
      lsum_or_minus if (p) { s = 0; for (; p; p = p->next) s += p->val; }
                    else s = -1; return s;   (control: -1 is not s's start)
      bytes_differ  ret = 0; for (; n > 0; n -= 1) ret |= *p1++ ^ *p2++;
                    return ret != 0;   (skip path `return 0`)
      count_report  n = 0; for (p = head; p; p = p->next) n++;
                    return report(head, n);   (skip path report(NULL, 0))
      count_or_one  if (!head) return report(head, 1); ... the same loop
                    (control: 1 is not n's start)
      visit         a bucket walk whose skip path assigns n = 0 in an else arm
      popcount_or   if (!x) return -1; c = 0; while (x) { x &= x - 1; c++; }
                    (control: the else arm assigns -1)
      free_opts     two counted loops sharing one counter register
      walk_keep     i = k; if (p) for (i = 0; p; p = p->next) i++; return i;
                    (control: the skip path returns k, not i's start)

    Pass 1 (default `proven`): dsum, bytes_differ, count_report, visit and
    free_opts print `while (c)` without their guards: the skip path's return,
    call or merged value is what the exit path gives when each carried
    variable keeps its entry value.  The four controls keep their guards and
    do-whiles.  Pass 2 (`option looptest binary`): every loop is a do-while
    behind its guard.
-->
